# patching-hosts host knob (#382). Grammar: skills/patching-hosts/references/knob.md
# (the vendored skill). The skill reads this file and never writes it. Times
# are UTC. A malformed line makes the host report-only until it is fixed.
# Held by tests/deploy/test_patching_knob.py: change a decision there first.

class production
posture scheduled

# --- when -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The owner's window, Sun 17:00-19:00 Pacific (decided 2026-10-23, epic #394;
# address-validator's slot). A knob time is UTC and the weekday is the UTC day
# the range starts, so it is Monday here: Sun 17:00 PST is Mon 01:00Z. Fixed in
# UTC, it reads Sun 18:00-20:00 PDT from 2027-03-14; move it then if the slot
# is meant to hold in Pacific time. Every step's whole span, the bulk's
# including the reboot, must fit inside it.
window Mon 01:00-03:00

# watcher-backup.timer: 03:17 UTC daily, RandomizedDelaySec=10min,
# AccuracySec=1min; the dump and upload take seconds. Outside the window
# today: kept so that widening the window can't put a step on the backup.
quiet 03:15-03:45
# watcher-cleanup.timer: Sun 03:00 (UTC on this host), RandomizedDelaySec=30min.
quiet 03:00-03:45 Sun

# --- the service ----------------------------------------------------------
# One process is the whole service: API, embedded Procrastinate worker and
# the bus consumers (AGENTS.md, Single process). Its restart is a full outage.
service watcher.service

# Procrastinate jobs in `doing`. A stop aborts what is left at 30 s (#334),
# well inside TimeoutStopSec, but a job cut off is retried, not finished: gate
# on none running. Read-only, as exedev; the opt-in names production for this
# one command, as every src/ops command does (#233).
inflight cd /home/exedev/watcher && WATCHER_ALLOW_PRODUCTION_DB=1 .venv/bin/python -m src.ops.inflight --env-file /etc/watcher/.env

# Loopback: uvicorn binds 0.0.0.0:8000. Assert the payload, not the status.
health curl -sf -m5 http://127.0.0.1:8000/health | jq -e '.status == "ok"'
health curl -sf -m5 http://127.0.0.1:8000/ready | jq -e '.status == "ready" and .db and .queue'

# --- the data store -------------------------------------------------------
# The cluster holds watcher, watcher_dev and watcher_test. Only watcher is
# production data; the other two are excepted below rather than declared,
# because the backup line stands in for the whole unit, and
# watcher-backup.service dumps watcher alone (--database watcher).
datastore postgres postgresql@16-main watcher
# The nightly dump to GCS (#296), create-only, checked in to co-status: the
# recovery point starts it and needs a fresh success instead of a second dump.
backup watcher-backup.service postgresql@16-main

# --- third-party origins --------------------------------------------------
# Each followed origin is scoped by a tracked pin file, installed under
# /etc/apt/preferences.d/ (deploy/apt-preferences.d/, docs/DEPLOYMENT.md).
# NodeSource: nodejs, for the Tailwind CLI (AGENTS.md).
origin deb.nodesource.com follow
# Tailscale carries the bus and notifier paths (docs/reference/tailscale.md).
# Its postinst restarts tailscaled; watcher.service orders After= it with no
# Wants=, so the restart is a bus outage, not a service stop: its own step.
# Its own auto-update is off for the tailnet (the owner, 2026-10-24) and goes
# off on the node in #382's host steps; the tailnet's default re-applies at a
# boot. The probe reads the node's at every run, so it moves only here.
origin pkgs.tailscale.com follow
hold tailscale tailscale-archive-keyring tailscale

# --- language dependencies -----------------------------------------------
# The service's venv is built from this repo's uv.lock, and the repo updates
# it. Named, because the remote is the deploy key's SSH alias, which the
# probe can't read as a GitHub repo.
owner /home/exedev/watcher self

# --- callers --------------------------------------------------------------
# None: nothing calls this host's API (the operator's dashboard aside), and
# every sibling reaches watcher over the bus (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).

# --- exceptions -----------------------------------------------------------
exception database:watcher_test 2027-04-30 the suite's database (tests/conftest.py), rebuilt every session; nothing in it to recover
exception database:watcher_dev 2027-04-30 a dev server's and the restore rehearsals' target (docs/RECOVERY-REHEARSALS.md); rebuilt from a production dump on demand
exception setup-script:redelivered 2027-04-30 contained in place, 600 root and exe-setup.service disabled, key revoked (watcher#331, watcher#347); delivery still re-runs at every boot (CannObserv/provisioner#4)
exception not-restarter:watcher-backup.service 2027-04-30 a DynamicUser running pg_dump, pg_restore and the GCS upload (src.ops.backup); starts nothing
exception not-restarter:watcher-cleanup.service 2027-04-30 runs as exedev, deleting caches (scripts/cleanup.sh); starts nothing
# No image-owner line: this repo is public and the image repo is not
# (gregoryfoster/skills#350).
